{
"opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the glom library, focusing on new specification types for data transformation and improved CLI capabilities. We are adding streaming support, better callable handling, and variable capture features, while ensuring all public specifier types have meaningful string representations.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m15",
"text": "The `glom_cli` command-line interface must accept Python-full specifications rather than just AST literals, allowing for more complex expression definitions in specs."
},
{
"id": "m29",
"text": "The public API must expose the `Auto`, `Fill`, `Iter`, `Let`, and `ROOT` names as specified, ensuring they are accessible for use in data transformation pipelines."
},
{
"id": "m33",
"text": "The `Invoke` class must provide a reasonable string representation that accurately reflects its state, particularly regarding its arguments."
},
{
"id": "m34",
"text": "The `Invoke` class must expose a `constants` attribute instead of `consts`, and internal implementation details like `args` should not be part of the public contract."
},
{
"id": "m44",
"text": "The `Fill` specifier must implement a `__repr__` method that returns a clear and descriptive string representation of the instance."
},
{
"id": "m45",
"text": "The `Assign` specifier and the `assign` convenience function must both provide reasonable string representations via their `__repr__` methods."
},
{
"id": "m46",
"text": "The `Coalesce` specifier and the `Inspect` specifier must both provide reasonable string representations via their `__repr__` methods."
},
{
"id": "m47",
"text": "All public specifier types, including `Auto` and `Check`, must have reasonable string representations that aid in debugging and introspection."
}
]
}
